## Step 1:  To simplify the expression, first distribute $(x+1)$ into each term of the first polynomial and each term of the third polynomial.
## Step 2:  Similarly, distribute $(x+1)$ into the terms of the second polynomial.
## Step 3:  After performing the distribution, group like terms together to simplify the expression.
## Step 4:  Combine like terms and rearrange the expression to form a polynomial.

First, we distribute $(x+1)$ into the terms of the first polynomial:
\begin{align*}
(2x^2+3x+7)(x+1)
&= 2x^3 + 3x^2 + 7x + 2x^2 + 3x + 7 \\
&= 2x^3 + 5x^2 + 10x + 7.
\end{align*}

## Step 5:  Next, distribute $(x+1)$ into the terms of the second polynomial:
\begin{align*}
-(x+1)(x^2+4x-63)
&=-x^3 - 4x^2 + 63x - x^2 - 4x + 63 \\
&=-x^3 - 5x^2 + 59x + 63.
\end{align*}

## Step 6:  Now, distribute $(x+1)$ into the terms of the third polynomial:
\begin{align*}
(3x-14)(x+1)(x+5)
&= (3x^2 - 11x - 14)(x+5)\\
&= 3x^3 - 11x^2 - 14x + 15x^2 - 55x - 70\\
&= 3x^3 + 4x^2 - 69x - 70.
\end{align*}

## Step 7:  Now we add the first and third terms together, then subtract the second term:
\begin{align*}
(2x^3+5x^2+10x+7)+(3x^3+4x^2-69x-70)-(-x^3 - 5x^2 + 59x + 63)
&= 2x^3 + 3x^3 - x^3 + 5x^2 + 4x^2 + 5x^2 - 5x^2 - 69x + 10x + 59x + 7 + 63 - 70
\end{align*}

## Step 8:  Combining like terms and simplifying gives us the polynomial
\begin{align*}
6x^3 + 8x^2 + 4x
\end{align*}

The final answer is: $\boxed{6x^3 + 8x^2 + 4x}$
